/**
 * Location-based landing pages — the typed matrix + copy builder.
 *
 * Programmatic SEO for the `(location) (service)` pattern, e.g. "London VPS
 * Hosting", "Toronto Web Hosting", "Frankfurt Game Server Hosting". The route
 * (`app/(marketing)/[slug]/page.tsx`) is driven entirely by this data table:
 * every page's H1, title, meta, OG, prose, why-points, steps, FAQ and internal
 * links are generated here from a (location × service) pair, so each page is
 * genuinely unique and market-specific rather than a thin doorway.
 *
 * Honesty note: Nxeon's production datacenter is Singapore. These pages are
 * written as *market-targeting* regional pages ("built to serve {city} and
 * {region}") — they never fabricate a per-city datacenter. The one location
 * with a real datacenter (Singapore) is flagged `presence: "datacenter"` and
 * gets first-person "we operate a datacenter here" copy; everywhere else the
 * copy is audience-first and the "where are the servers" FAQ is answered
 * truthfully. See `presence` below.
 */

